      <div type="clause" n="8.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ICn">I Cn</ref> 8.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="8.2" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="292" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ gyf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.1"/> hwa þonne þa teoþunge gelæstan nelle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.2"/>, swa we gecweden<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.3"/> habbað, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> is se teoða æcer, ealswa seo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.4"/> sulh hit gegá<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.5"/>, þonne fare þæs<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.6"/> cingces gerefa to ⁊ þæs bisceopes ⁊ þæs landrican ⁊ þæs mynstres mæssepreost, ⁊ nime<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.star"/> unþances ðone<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.7"/> teoðan dæl to þam mynstre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.8"/>, þe hit to gebyrige<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.9"/>; ⁊ tæcan him to þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> nigoðan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.10"/> dæle, ⁊ todæle mann<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.11"/> þa eahta dælas on twa, ⁊ fo se landhlaford to healfum, to<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.12"/> healfu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> se bisceop, si hit ciningces mann, se<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.13"/> hit þegnes.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="8.2" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="292" ed="#liebermann"/>And gyf hwa þonne þa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.1-3"/> teoþunge gelæstan nelle, swa we gecweden habbaþ<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.2-4"/>, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> is se teoða æcer, ealswa seo sulh hit gegað, þonne fare to þæs cyninges gerefa ⁊ þas biscopas ⁊ þæs landrican ⁊ þæs mynstres mæssepreost, ⁊ niman unþances þonne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.3-3"/> teoðan dæl to þam mynstre, þe hit to gebirige; ⁊ teacan him to þam nigoðum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.4-4"/> dæle, ⁊ todæle man þa eahta dælas on twa, ⁊ fo se landhlaford to healfum, to healfan se biscop, sy hyt cyninges man, sy hit þegnes.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="8.2" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="292" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis hanc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.2-2"/> decimam dare nolit, sicut<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.3-2"/> omnium nostrum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.4-2"/> commune est institutum, hoc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.5-2"/> est decima acra, sicut aratrum peragrabit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.6-2"/>, eat prepositus regis et episcopi et ipsius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.7-2"/> terrę domini cum sacerdote, et ingratis auferant et ęcclesię cui pertinebit reddant; nonam uero partem relinquant<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.8-2"/> ei qui decimam dare noluit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.9-2"/>; octo partes reliquas in duo diuidant, et sit una medietas<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.10-2"/> episcopi, alia<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.11-2"/> terrę domini, siue regis homo sit siue taini.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="8.2" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="293" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis decimam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.5-4"/>, sicut carruca perarat, dare noluerit, adeant<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.6-3"/> eum prępositus regis et prępositus episcopi, prępositus etiam domini, cuius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.7-3"/> in capite terra est, et presbyter ęcclesię, ad quam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.8-3"/> decima illa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.9-3"/> pertinet (eant<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.10-3"/>), et, si aliter non possunt, ui auferant decimam et dent ęcclesię, ad quam (iuste<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.11-3"/>) pertinet; nonam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.12-2"/> autem partem dimittant<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.13-2"/> illi (dent ei), qui iniuste decimam retinuit; octo uero partes diuidantur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.14"/> inter dominum terrę et episcopum, cuiuscunque homo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.15"/> sit, regis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.16"/>, comitis aut liberalis hominis, quem Angli þegen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.oe.17"/> uocant.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="8.2" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="293" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis autem hanc decimacionem, sicut prediximus, soluere repugnauerit (ea est decimum iugum, sicut arauerit), adeat prepositus regis cum preposito episcopi et preposito ipsius domini terre, necnon [presbiter] ipsius ecclesie, ad quam decimacio attinet; qui inuito decimam illam auferant ecclesieque reddant et nonam partem tantum illi dimittant; octoque partes equaliter diuidant, quarum altera quidem domino, altera uero contingat episcopo, cuiuscumque homo ipse sit, siue episcopi siue regis siue uirronis.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="8.2" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="164" ed="#robertson"/>⁊ gyf hwa þonne þa teoþunge gelæstan nelle swa we gecweden habbað, þæt is se teoða æcer ealswa seo sulh hit gegá<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#ICn_8-2.robnote.fn.1"/>, þonne fare þæs cingces gerefa to ⁊ þæs bisceopes ⁊ þæs landrican ⁊ þæs mynstres mæssepreost ⁊ nim[an]<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#ICn_8-2.robnote.fn.2"/> unþances ðone<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#ICn_8-2.robnote.fn.3"/> teoðan dæl to þam mynstre þe hit to gebyrige, ⁊ tæcan him to þam nigoðan dæle, ⁊ todæle mann þa eahta dælas on twa, ⁊ fo se landhlaford to healfum, to healfum se bisceop, si hit ciningces mann, se hit þegnes.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="242" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And gyf hwa þonne þa teoþunge gelæstan nelle swa we gecweden habbað—þæt is se teoða æcer, ealswa seo sulh hit gega—þonne fare þæs cingces gerefa to, and þæs bisceopes and þæs landrican and þæs mynstres mæssepreost, and niman unþances ðone teoðan dæl to þam mynstre þe hit to gebyrige, and tæcan him to þam nigoðan dæle, and todæle mann þa eahta dælas on twa, and fo se landhlaford to healfum, to healfum se bisceop, si hit ciningces mann se hit þegnes.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="293" ed="#liebermann"/>Und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.de.1"/> wenn nun einer die Zehnten, wie wir verordnet haben, zu leisten sich weigert — nämlich [je]der<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.de.2"/> zehnte Acker, wie der Pflug es überschreitet —, dann ziehe zu [ihm hin] der Königsvogt und [der] des Bischofs und [der] des Immunitätsherrn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.de.3"/> und der Pfarrer der [berechtigten] Kirche, und sie nehmen gegen seinen Willen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.de.4"/> für diese Kirche, der es zukommt, den Zehnten fort und weisen ihn zum neunten Zehntel; und vertheile man die [übrigen] acht Zehntel in zwei [Hälften], und ergreife der Immunitätsherr die Hälfte, die Hälfte der Bischof, sei es [der Weigerer] ein Vasall des Königs, sei es eines Adligen.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#ICn_8-2.lnote.de.5"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And if anyone then refuses to pay the tithe as we have ordained — namely [every] tenth acre, as the plough passes over it —, then let the king's reeve and the bishop's [reeve] and the [reeve] of the lord of the immunity and the priest of the [entitled] minster go [to him], and take the tenth part against his will for the minster to which it belongs, and assign him the ninth part; and let the [remaining] eight parts be divided in two, and let the landlord take half, the bishop half, whether [the refuser] is the king's man or a thegn's.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-g-a"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#ICn_8-2.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="165" ed="#robertson"/>And if anyone refuses to render his tithes as we have decreed, namely, the produce of every tenth acre traversed by the plough, then the king's reeve and the bishop's and the reeve of the lord of the manor and the priest of the church shall go, and, without his consent, take the tenth part for the church to which it is due, and shall assign the next tenth to him, and the eight [remaining] parts shall be divided in two, and the lord of the manor shall take half and the bishop half, whether the man be under the lordship of the king or of a thegn.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="243" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And if anyone refuses to pay his tithes in the manner that we have decreed—that is, a one-tenth yield of every acre traversed by the plow—then the king’s reeve and the reeves of the bishop and landlord and the priest of the church are to go and forfeit without consent a one-tenth portion for the church to which it belongs, and the next tenth is to be left for the recreant, and the remaining eight-tenths are to be divided in two and the landlord shall receive half and the bishop the other half, whether he is a king’s man or a thane’s.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="293"><ref target="clause:IIEg_3-1">II Eg 3.1</ref>; <ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_7">VIII Atr 7</ref>; <ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_8">VIII Atr 8</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. II Eg. 3, 1; VIII Atr. 7 | ebd. 8</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:IIEg_3-1">II Eg 3.1</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, I Cn 8:2: (HomN L) VIII Atr 7-8  II Eg 3:1</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><label>quoted verbatim (bold in Wormald's table)</label> <ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_7">VIII Atr 7–8</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, I Cn 8:2: (HomN L) VIII Atr 7-8  II Eg 3:1</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="38"><label>word for word</label> <ref target="clause:IIEg_3-1">II Eg 3.1</ref> <quote>then let the king's reeve and the bishop's and the landlord's (landrican) and the minster's mass-priest go there ...[word-for word as excerpt 3.]</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">G's ‘nime’ should be ‘niman’ (other MSS, II Eg, VIII Atr); G's ‘se hit’ is so in G (= ‘sy hit’). Liebermann compares II Eg 3.1; VIII Atr 7 f.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 293, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">gega: gegað A</note>
