        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_8-2.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">200</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Benutzt durch Hn 11, 2</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Used by Hn 11, 2</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_8-2.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">200</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nominativ syntaktisch anstössig [Schmid], wohl weil aus anderer Quelle ungenügend redigiert</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Nominative syntactically objectionable [Schmid], probably because inadequately edited from another source</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_8-2.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">200</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Dieser fehlte Eg; Cnut anerkennt die seit Atr eingeführte private Gerichtsbarkeit des Adels, den Inst mit Normann. Terminus als Kronlehnträger bezeichnet; Cn meinte gewiss nicht bloss solchen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">This was lacking in Eg; Cnut recognizes the private jurisdiction of the nobility, introduced since Atr, which Inst designates with a Norman term as tenants-in-chief; Cn certainly did not mean these alone</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_8-2.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">200</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nur im Notfall; Inst</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Only in case of necessity; Inst</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="ICn_8-2.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">200</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Als typische Lehnsherren zwischen König und Thegn bezeichnet Inst den Grafen, Cons den Bischof</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">As the typical feudal lord between king and thegn, Inst names the earl, Cons the bishop</seg></note>
